docs {
  # shoes API: integration tests

  Integration tests for the `shoes` catalog service. Run the folders in order (01 to 06): together they
  create one product, read it back, filter it, update it, attach images, fetch reviews and delete it
  again, then check that requests without a valid token are refused. `06-system` reads `GET /system`.

  Every run uses a fresh suffix (`{{run}}`, set by `01-products/01 Create product`) in product names and
  SKUs, so the collection can run again and again against the same database, even next to other data.

  Image uploads read `../assets/*.png` and `../assets/notes.txt`, relative to this folder.

  The reviews requests need internet access: the service fetches reviews from jsonplaceholder.typicode.com.

  Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (set below, inherited by each request with
  `auth: inherit`). The service accepts any token of exactly 10 characters; `environments/local.bru` sets
  `token` to `test-token`. `05-authentication` sends its own headers to check the 401 responses.
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}
